WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.789
Could you, could sketch 

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.669
what's wrong

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:28.080
from your perspective

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.440
with subjective rights,

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.690
right, you're one of the sharpest critics

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:38.570
from theological circles in, in, in the kind of

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.700
Christian theological circles of subjective rights that are kind of

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:41.680
underpin

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.990
the whole liberal democracy. That's a,
that's a huge challenge, right.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:53.080
And so it may be helpful if you would, if you would sketch in a few points 

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:59.100
what is, what you see as a problem with that. Maybe that's going to generate our discussion.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.240
I know that we read some of that, but, but if you could maybe

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.960
remind us of it that would be helpful.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.220
Well I think

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.400
they most generally speaking, they,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.240
they, they, they place the focus wrongly in trying to understand

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.240
human community,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.650
what

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:21.580
theologically speaking I would refer to as moral community,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:27.189
that is to say, the whole community of human goods and rights, not using the term "moral" in any narrow sense.

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:30.880
I think they misplace the focus.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.430
It ought to be on

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.700
human relationships with God

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.100
and with one another

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.659
and not on individuals.

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:41.409
That is the first point.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:42.280
The, the, the, 

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.190
stemming from that

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:48.420
is the question, "Well, why

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.350
this focus on the individual?"

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.820
And as I make, I've made this point, of course, in my, in my 

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.620
interpretation of the history of Western rights

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.480
and again today that I think that focus has had from the beginning

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.070
had

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.959
an interest in seeing human

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:10.350
freedom, that is to

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.529
say, the, the capacity of human beings to choose

00:02:14.529 --> 00:02:16.689
to do one thing rather than another,

00:02:16.689 --> 00:02:20.859
to make one moral judgment rather than another, one judgment rather than

00:02:20.859 --> 00:02:22.879
another, that very capacity

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:26.549
has been seen as the, an originating right 

00:02:26.549 --> 00:02:28.129
on which all other

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:29.339
human rights

00:02:29.339 --> 00:02:31.529
are based,

00:02:31.529 --> 00:02:34.720
erected, the foundation of the building of human rights.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.889
And that is the case I think from the canonists onward,

00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:43.909
that is not simply part of, one might sa,y

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:46.109
the Lockean-Hobesian project, the, the later project.

00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:49.280
And the

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.659
understanding of the individual

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:53.639
as a proprietor,

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.739
someone who

00:02:55.739 --> 00:02:57.060
both,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:57.549
who,

00:02:57.549 --> 00:03:00.360
who governs him or herself

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.479
precisely because they own

00:03:02.479 --> 00:03:03.929
their

00:03:03.929 --> 00:03:08.159
capacities and spiritual resources and they own their

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:10.829
acts. In a sense they make their

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:13.400
acts and they have a proprietary

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.839
control to dispose of

00:03:14.839 --> 00:03:19.280
the, a proprietary right to dispose of themselves and their acts as they,

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.419
they wish to.

00:03:20.419 --> 00:03:22.689
This, this is a,

00:03:22.689 --> 00:03:25.480
a conception which implicit

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.879
and, and

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:30.489
drawn-out has accompanied the path of Western human rights

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:33.579
more or less from the beginning 

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:39.689
in, in, in various stages of sort of explicit-ness and

00:03:39.689 --> 00:03:42.370
elaboration. And that it seems to me

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:49.370
runs clean contrary to an understanding of human beings as essentially

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:52.709
oriented in

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:54.769
their,

00:03:54.769 --> 00:03:57.769
their communal and individual lives

00:03:57.769 --> 00:03:59.789
to their relationship to God,

00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:03.049
and, to, to

00:04:03.049 --> 00:04:06.219
their neighbors.

00:04:06.219 --> 00:04:08.789
Their relationship to God

00:04:08.789 --> 00:04:10.709
being one,

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:11.709
as I indicated

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:13.160
a few moments ago,

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.289
being one

00:04:14.289 --> 00:04:15.789
primarily

00:04:15.789 --> 00:04:18.660
of, of adoration,

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.750
love, gratitude,

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.440
reverence, and

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.159
openness and obedience

00:04:24.159 --> 00:04:25.170
in the sense of openness

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.639
to

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:28.710
divine,

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:32.090
the divine will as it reveals itself both in

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:38.610
our natural perceptions of right and also as revealed to Christians in Scripture.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.950
So,

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.130
the main point really is

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.610
about the misplaced focus

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:50.020
and from there one can go on to, to

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.399
a,

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.860
a spectrum

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.440
of theological

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.090
and philosophical criticisms.

